# The := slice (the book, named-actuals): a named actual `zz := 5` names a formal the selected callable does not have --
# the refusal of the call at translation, before any argument is computed.
fn: tst (int: c 3; int: a 2) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: tst
int: code 7
if: tst(zz := 5) != 35
    code := 81
---
send: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
